Problem 2(b) - Structure of the supplied module template
The template contains a module-level docstring at the top, imports near the beginning of the file, function definitions, function-level docstrings, examples, and comments. The module docstring explains the purpose of the file. Imports are kept at the top so that all dependencies used by the functions are clear. Each function has its own docstring that explains what it does, its parameters, its return value, and an example. Comments make the code easier to follow. The example section is also useful for testing with doctest.

Problem 2(c-d) - Cleaning the template and starting square
I copied the supplied module template and removed imports and example material that were not needed for this assignment. I kept NumPy because the functions operate on numerical arrays and Matplotlib pyplot because squareplot creates a plot. I then replaced the example function with a function named square.

